    "summary": "Cloth, an imported cotton cloth with a plaid pattern similar to Af1981,11.5. This was composed of brown warps and yellow, purple and white wefts. This combination of warps and wefts would have originally created two panels of yellow and white grids on a purple background bordered by check. It has been adapted by the Kalabari by cutting out sections to create a design known as CROSS and DRAUGHT. The cloth has not been hemmed.",
